# Pitfalls (each one observed and measured)

| Pitfall | What happened | Do instead |
|---|---|---|
| **Decorating fixed massing** | Trim knobs on procedural shophouses passed every check and barely changed the look | Change the form (concept/type program); name the term that blocks it |
| **Mesh as substrate** | Image→3D mesh→voxels: every surface inherited from the mesh failed; re-authored surfaces passed; seven epics were lost tuning a judge on a broken seed | Use references as *evidence* for recognition; author the build |
| **Style collapse** | Every build converged to one rustic grammar because nothing penalised it | Derive identity from context every time |
| **Over-decoration** | Bands on every floor = stripes; alternating quoins = checkerboard; a "more detail" push turned colour monochrome | Restraint, rest areas, one strong line |
| **Recolour ≠ construction** | Repainting a wall plane added no depth | Things proud / recessed |
| **Floating parts** | Freestanding columns copied from a reference floated in front of the facade | Engage everything with the wall |
| **Concealment** | Filling a hole raised a score by hiding the defect | Fix the cause; replace, don't patch |
| **Wrong critique view** | A revise pass that saw only a flat head-on elevation removed 1,000 blocks and regressed | Critique from eye height / inside / 3/4 views |
| **Second pass as a coin flip** | Revisions helped some runs and hurt others; unprompted "improve it" rounds lost to the first build in blind picks | Revise only on a person's comment; keep every version, compare, keep the better |
| **Capped ambition** | Builds landed exactly on whatever size/relief limit the prompt stated | State the bar high; check you used the room |
| **Guessing host rules** | A brief named the wrong side as the party wall; the model left the visible side plain | Read the host's data/rules before briefing |
| **Unchecked protection** | Removing a guard broke 57 reserved cells and every other check stayed green | Break each protection on purpose once; a rule must fail first |
| **Self-reported effort** | A subagent said "about 25 minutes"; it took 6 | Measure |
| **Single numeric judge** | VLM scores swung 0–76 on the same render; a rubric saturated at "strong" for everything | Pairwise before/after and your own glance |
